  "inspected_evidence": [
    "Weeks et al.1953: complete 7 pages, Figures1-3 and Tables1-3; natural specimens, separation, chemistry and impurity limits.",
    "Evans and Block1953: complete 9 pages; sharp and diffuse lattices, specimen provenance and interpreted Fe compensation. Corrected calculated factors are not reused.",
    "Evans and Mrose1955: complete 15 pages including printed Tables1-5 and Figures1-4, source data and alteration inference. Page867 correction was visually enlarged and verified as k odd.",
    "Curetti and Pavese2023: complete 10-page published PDF, all9 figures and all4 tables, publisher HTML/XML and four table workbooks. Workbook ZIP/XML contents were opened into table-workbook-cells.json. The inspected assets page lists no separate supplement; the advertised deposited-data route is CCDC.",
    "IMA September2026: definitions and license pages1-2; montroseite row PDF147 and paramontroseite row PDF165 visually checked. Navajoite and pascoite rows were used for candidate triage only.",
    "USGS TEI4391954: acquired and text-extracted as the predecessor of the1955 study, not an independent experiment.",
    "Navajoite1955 and Evans/Hughes1990: acquired. The later paper pages517-519 was inspected for deferred identity hazards, without full scientific acceptance.",
    "Pascoite2005: complete8-page PDF acquired; abstract, introduction and deposited-table statement inspected for a deferred source handoff, without full scientific acceptance."
  ],
  "claim_limits": [
    "The1953 mineral description has no isolated pure endmember. Bitter Creek chemistry is a partial analysis of120mg; Matchless and Whitney samples are impure. Inferred bulk phase proportions are not timed conversion or recovery.",
    "The1955 natural crystals are intergrowths;99 and34 visually estimated reflections were used without absorption correction, and diffuse-phase data were poor. Weathering below50 degrees C and hydrogen migration are inferred, without controlled kinetics or direct hydrogen tracking. Diffuse A remains unidentified.",
    "The1955 page867 footnote corrects1953 Table2 calculated factors for k odd and changes R from0.21 to0.11. The1955 montroseite data reuse1953 measurements, and the1954 report precedes1955 publication.",
    "The2023 Fe-rich Prachovice specimen differs from Colorado material and pure VO2. Measured average chemistry, refined occupancies and the approximate Al-free reaction formula differ. Cation valence is inferred from composition and structure rather than directly measured.",
    "The2023 powder retains about8wt% calcite. Methods do not specify gas composition, flow or oxygen fugacity. Heating used20 degrees C/min,50-degree steps,2-hour holds and approximately150-minute diffraction scans. The6-hour/400-degree-C crystal analyses are separate arms.",
    "The2023 section3.2 final proportions of about65wt% Fe2V4O13 and35wt% V2O5 conflict with Figure7, whose labeled bars show larger V2O5 and retained calcite. No exact final product fraction or recovery yield is adopted. Figure7 ends500 degrees C, methods state550, and Table3 ends450.",
    "The2023 Raman laser alters crystals; overlapping peaks and an unavailable Fe2V4O13 reference prevent unique assignment. No rutile-type VO2 was observed under this powder protocol. Absence of an amorphous intermediate is an indirect inference from the internal calcite reference.",
    "CCDC2212426 and2212427 are paper-reported deposits; bounded legitimate access routes returned404. No CIF/FCF acquisition or authority resolution is claimed, and these are not root material identifiers.",
    "Bounded web queries and Crossref metadata did not surface an additional publisher-linked correction or retraction for2023. This is not an exhaustive absence claim. The actual1955 correction and2023 internal inconsistencies are retained.",
    "No microbial mechanism, inherited species criticality, isolated vanadium product or industrial recovery is established by the curated sources."
  ],
